 <v:imagedata croptop="-65520f" cropbottom="65520f"/>
</v:shape><span style='mso-element:field-end'></span><![endif]--></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc218145348"><![if !supportLists]><span style='mso-fareast-font-family:
Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>1<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Installation</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal>IP Pascal can be installed and run on computers meeting the
following requirements.</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l9 level1 lfo4'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Windows XP, Windows XP Pro, Windows NT, or
Windows 2000, or server versions</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l9 level1 lfo4'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>80586 or better CPU (Intel refers to the 80586
as &quot;Pentium&quot;)</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l9 level1 lfo4'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>CD-ROM drive</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l9 level1 lfo4'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Hard disk with at least 20megabytes of free
space</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>IP Pascal will require activation to function. This can be
done automatically via Internet connection, or alternately you can manually
process the activation yourself via email. No personal information is passed
during activation. The activation server receives numbers validating your copy
of IP Pascal, and the numbers that verify your Windows installation on your
computer.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>IP Pascal is supplied on an ISO standard CD-ROM. It needs to
be directly installed from the original CD-ROM.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>To start the installation, please insert the CD-ROM
containing IP Pascal into an available drive on the target machine. If the
installation does not start automatically, please perform the following
procedure</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo5'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Press the &quot;start&quot; button in the lower
left hand corner</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo5'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Click the &quot;My Computer&quot; icon</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo5'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Right click the icon for the CD-ROM drive you
inserted IP Pascal into</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo5'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Select &quot;Explore&quot; from the menu list on
the drive</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo5'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Click &quot;Setup&quot; in the contents of the
drive</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The installation program should then start. You may then see
the &quot;loading&quot; screen. This is normal.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:27.15pt'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_1" o:spid="_x0000_i1064" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install1.bmp"
 style='width:324.75pt;height:223.5pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image005.png" o:title="install1"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=433 height=298
src="manual_files/image006.jpg" alt=install1.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_1"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When the installer is finished loading, you will see:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.0cm'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_2" o:spid="_x0000_i1063" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install2.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image007.png" o:title="install2"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image008.jpg" alt=install2.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_2"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Hit &quot;Next&quot; to continue.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:27.15pt'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_3" o:spid="_x0000_i1062" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install3.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image009.png" o:title="install3"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image010.jpg" alt=install3.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_3"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>On this screen you can read the complete end user license
for IP Pascal. Please scroll through and read the entire license, then indicate
your acceptance by hitting the &quot;I Agree&quot; button. Selecting this
button indicates you accept and have read this license. If you do NOT agree
with the terms of the license, you may hit &quot;Cancel&quot;, repackage IP
Pascal including the CD-ROM, this manual, and all related material, and return
it to Moore/CAD for a full refund.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When you hit the &quot;I Agree&quot; button, the
&quot;Next&quot; button will appear. After pressing this:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:27.15pt'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_4" o:spid="_x0000_i1061" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install4.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image011.png" o:title="install4"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image012.jpg" alt=install4.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_4"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>On this page, you may specify the installation location. If
the default installation location is acceptable, you may just hit the
&quot;Next&quot; button. Otherwise, you may edit the default install location,
then hit the &quot;Next&quot; button.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:27.15pt'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_5" o:spid="_x0000_i1060" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install5.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image013.png" o:title="install5"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image014.jpg" alt=install5.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_5"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The search path is used by the command line processor
cmd.exe to find IP Pascal program components. If you don't plan to run IP
Pascal from the command line, you can skip this stage, by unchecking the
&quot;Modify Search Path&quot; checkbox. If you leave the box checked and hit
&quot;Next&quot; you will see:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:27.15pt'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_6" o:spid="_x0000_i1059" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install6.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image015.png" o:title="install6"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image016.jpg" alt=install6.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_6"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The installer will add the IP Pascal program path to the end
of your existing program path. If you want to see the entire new path, and it
is too long to be displayed (as above), simply click within the edit window and
use the arrow, end and home keys to see the entire path.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Hit &quot;next&quot; to continue.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:27.15pt'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_7" o:spid="_x0000_i1058" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install6.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image017.png" o:title="install6"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image018.jpg" alt=install6.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_7"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>On this page you will select automatic or manual
installation. It will be automatic by default. If you wish to install manually,
you may uncheck the &quot;automatically Activate IP Pascal&quot; checkbox and
hit &quot;Next&quot;.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>If your computer has no access to the Internet, you will
see:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:27.15pt'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_8" o:spid="_x0000_i1057" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install8.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image019.png" o:title="install8"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image020.jpg" alt=install8.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_8"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>In this case, you must hit the &quot;Back&quot; button,
uncheck the &quot;Automatically Activate IP Pascal&quot; button and continue.
For manual activations, you will see:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:27.15pt'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_9" o:spid="_x0000_i1056" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install9.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image021.png" o:title="install9"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image022.jpg" alt=install9.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_9"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The product signature shown is a &quot;hash&quot; that
consists of numbers identifying the IP Pascal software, your installation of
Windows, and your computer. No personal information is sent. This same product
signature that you see is the data that is exchanged automatically with the
Internet server.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>From the time you see the product signature, you have 30
minutes to complete the activation. If you don't complete activation within
that time, don't worry. You can simply start the installation over again and
get a new product signature.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>To manually activate IP Pascal, send the entire 39 character
signature in the body of an email, with any subject, to:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>activation@moorecad.com</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>This is connected to an automated email processor, and it
will email you a reply that has a 39 digit reply in it.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Hit &quot;Next&quot;.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.0cm'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_10" o:spid="_x0000_i1055" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install10.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image023.png" o:title="install10"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image024.jpg" alt=install10.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_10"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>On this page, you will enter the reply you received from the
server.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Hit next.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>If the code was not correct, you will see the page:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.0cm'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_11" o:spid="_x0000_i1054" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install11.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image025.png" o:title="install11"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image026.jpg" alt=install11.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_11"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>If this occurs, simply recheck the activation reply
carefully for the same digits, and number of digits. Note that you can cut and
paste the activation reply directly into the edit box.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When this is complete, you will see:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.0cm'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_0" o:spid="_x0000_i1053" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install12.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image027.png" o:title="install12"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image028.jpg" alt=install12.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_0"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.0cm'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_12" o:spid="_x0000_i1052" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install13.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image029.png" o:title="install13"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image030.jpg" alt=install13.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_12"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Hit &quot;Next&quot;.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Now you are ready to install IP Pascal. Simply hit
&quot;Next&quot; to begin the installation.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.0cm'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_13" o:spid="_x0000_i1051" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install14.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image031.png" o:title="install14"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image032.jpg" alt=install14.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_13"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.0cm'><span style='mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape
 id="Picture_x0020_14" o:spid="_x0000_i1050" type="#_x0000_t75" alt="install15.bmp"
 style='width:323.25pt;height:203.25pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="manual_files/image033.png" o:title="install15"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=431 height=271
src="manual_files/image034.jpg" alt=install15.bmp v:shapes="Picture_x0020_14"><![endif]></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Now your installation is complete. You can hit
&quot;Exit&quot; or close the installer to terminate.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>In order to complete your installation, if you plan to use
command line tools (cmd.exe), you need to reboot the system to resyncronize
Windows to the new environment.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

