<h1><a name="_Toc218145357"><![if !supportLists]><span style='mso-fareast-font-family:
Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>3<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Implementation
Defined Behavior</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal>To use IP Pascal in a strictly ISO 7185 compatible mode, you
will need to know the information in this chapter. It contains all of the
details of the standard that are left implementation defined.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The implementation defined characteristics of IP Pascal in
summary are:</p>

<p class=tableheader0>Language Construct<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>IP
Pascal Detail<span class=MsoIntenseReference><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;font-variant:normal !important;
color:#C00000;letter-spacing:0pt;font-weight:normal'><o:p></o:p></span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Maxint<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                                       </span>2147483647.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Format of integer<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                       </span>32
bit 2's complement binary.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Character set<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                             </span>American
ASCII 7 bit, stored and processed as 8 bit. The 8th bit is ignored in source
files.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Elements in a set<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                       </span>256,
numbered as 0 to 255.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Maximum size of source line<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>    </span>200
characters.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Maximum size of labels<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>200
characters (one full line).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Size of real<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                                </span>-1.8e308
to +1.8e308.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Format of real<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                           </span>64
bit IEEE standard 754</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Appearance of exponent<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>           </span>The
exponent character is lower case &quot;e&quot;.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>File I/O<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                                      </span>Uses
&quot;lazy I/O&quot;, allowing for interactive files.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Values written for boolean<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>        </span>Lower
case &quot;false&quot; and lower case &quot;true&quot;.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>Maximum size for any</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>structure, program, or program</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:148.85pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-148.85pt;line-height:
normal'>section<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                                       </span>Limited
only by the size of the address space for the processor.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The following default field widths are used:</p>

<p class=tableheader0>Type<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>               </span>Field
(characters)<span class=MsoIntenseReference><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;font-variant:normal !important;
color:#C00000;letter-spacing:0pt;font-weight:normal'><o:p></o:p></span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>Integer<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>             </span>11</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>Boolean<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>           </span>5</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>Character<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>         </span>1</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>Real<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                 </span>22</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>IP Pascal is implemented in 32 bits. The value of maxint is
2147483647. The compiler uses ASCII 7 bit encoding throughout, both in the
compiler and in the generated code. However, the compiler accepts any character
code in the range 0..255, and will leave such codes intact.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>ASCII control characters (characters with values between 0
and 32) are treated as equivalent to spaces in the compiler and it's runtime
utilities. Any control characters may be used to format source without effect
on the compilation (for example, inclusion of form-feeds).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Sets are implemented as having from 1..256 elements, so that
all of the ASCII characters, as well as other specially defined characters in
the range 0..255 can be represented as a set. Only ordinals in the range 0..255
can be represented in a set.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The maximum size of any array or structure, the size of a
generated program, the size of any local or global data area, is limited only
by available memory. The maximum size of program or procedure, maximum nesting
level of included files that can be compiled is limited only by available
memory.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The maximum size of the command line acceptable, the maximum
size of any source line, string constant, program label or goto label, is 250
characters.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The format of the standard type real is a 64 bit IEEE
standard real format. It can represent numbers in the range -1.8e308..+1.8e308.
The exponent character output for reals is a lower case &quot;e&quot;.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Files under IP Pascal are implemented using the &quot;lazy
I/O&quot; method, which makes IP Pascal applicable to interactive applications.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The strings output for boolean are output in lower case.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The types:</p>

<p class=Code>Text</p>

<p class=Code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>and</p>

<p class=Code>file of char</p>

<p class=Code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Are not equivalent, as allowed for by the standard. Only on
a text file may writeln, readln, eoln and conversions to/from ascii format be
applied. A file of char is simply a file whose elements are characters, without
special interpretation, including control characters, and including the
characters that normally make up the end of line sequence.</p>

<h2><a name="_Toc218145358"><![if !supportLists]><span style='mso-fareast-font-family:
Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>3.1<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Additional
reserved words</a></h2>

<p class=MsoNormal>The following identifiers are added as reserved under IP
Pascal, and may not appear as program identifiers, unless the
&quot;standard&quot; option is enabled:</p>

<p class=tableheader0 style='page-break-after:avoid'>Additional Reserved Words<span
class=MsoIntenseReference><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;font-variant:normal !important;color:#C00000;
letter-spacing:0pt;font-weight:normal'><o:p></o:p></span></span></p>

<p class=reference style='margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;page-break-after:
avoid'>Module<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>           </span>process<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>          </span>monitor<span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>          </span>share<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>              </span>uses</p>

<p class=reference style='margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;page-break-after:
avoid'>private<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>external<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>          </span>forward<span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>          </span>xor<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>                  </span>view</p>

<p class=reference style='margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;page-break-after:
avoid'>fixed<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>    </span><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>            </span>class<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>   </span><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>atom<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>               </span>construct<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>       </span>destruct</p>

<p class=reference style='margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>is<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                     </span>overload<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>         </span>override</p>

<p class=reference style='margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Note that the words forward and external are reserved words
under IP Pascal. They perform the same function as the equivalent directives
under standard Pascal, and so maintain compliance with the standard.</p>

<h2><a name="_Toc218145359"><![if !supportLists]><span style='mso-fareast-font-family:
Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>3.2<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Header
File Linkage</a></h2>

<p class=MsoNormal>The standard leaves the linkage of header files to external
files as undefined, except in the case of the input and output files. IP Pascal
also implements the header files error and list, and the meaning of these files
is as follows:</p>

<p class=tableheader0 style='page-break-after:avoid'>File Identifier<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>             </span>Meaning<span
class=MsoIntenseReference><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;font-variant:normal !important;color:#C00000;
letter-spacing:0pt;font-weight:normal'><o:p></o:p></span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:106.35pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-106.35pt;page-break-after:
avoid'>input<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                            </span>Input
from the user console, or redirected</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:106.35pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-106.35pt;page-break-after:
avoid'>output<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                          </span>Output
to the user console, or redirected.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:106.35pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-106.35pt;page-break-after:
avoid'>error<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                            </span>Output
to the user console, not redirected.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:106.35pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-106.35pt;mso-pagination:
lines-together'>list<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>                               </span>Output
to the default printing device. Requires a page to be executed on the file
before output will appear.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:4.0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-4.0cm;page-break-after:
avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The error and list files share the property of the input and
output files that they need not be declared, and are by default type text.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Files that appear in the header other than the above names
are automatically linked to external files via the command line. See section
3.15. These files must be typed in the program as specified in the standard,
and will be treated as byte files mapped into the element type of the file. The
exact mapping of each type to a byte file is processor dependent, and you will
need to consult the processor implementation information in this manual to
determine it. However, the following types are universal to any processor
implementation:</p>

<p class=tableheader0>Type <span style='mso-tab-count:3'>                          </span>Mapping<span
class=MsoIntenseReference><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;font-variant:normal !important;color:#C00000;
letter-spacing:0pt;font-weight:normal'><o:p></o:p></span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:4.0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-4.0cm'>text<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>                                </span>American ASCII
characters in 8 bit bytes, with end of line and end of file formatting.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:4.0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-4.0cm'>file of char<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>                    </span>American ASCII characters in
8 bit bytes, without any formatting.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:4.0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-4.0cm'>file of 0..255<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>                 </span>Bytes.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:4.0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-4.0cm'>file of -128..127<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>Bytes.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>In addition to requiring a type, nonstandard header files
need to be specifically reset or rewritten using reset and rewrite. These files
close automatically with the program end, and are preserved after file
completion in their command line specified names.</p>

<h2><a name="_Toc218145360"><![if !supportLists]><span style='mso-fareast-font-family:
Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>3.3<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Interactions
Between Standard and Extended Language</a></h2>

<p class=MsoNormal>To use IP as a completely standards obeying implementation,
the standard mode switch is recommended (see section 4.2).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>It is, however possible to leave the standard switch off and
compile completely standard programs. IP Pascal is specifically designed so
that the extended features do not interfere with the standard language
features. It is also possible to make minimal use of extended features if
desired, as the extended features use types and methods defined in the
standard. For example, opening files by name allows use of a standard Pascal
string type.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The exception to this is the extended keywords of IP Pascal.
The extra keywords, covered in section 3.1.2, must not be used in standard
conforming source with the standard switch off. In addition, the directives <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>forward</span></span> and <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>external</span></span> are promoted to reserved
words in the IP Pascal language.</p>

<span style='font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:"Times New Roman","serif";
mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:
minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:
AR-SA'><br clear=all style='mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:
always'>
</span>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

